// A string inside a hole may have holes of its own. A quote inside a hole
// that its line never closes is read as the closer of the string around
// the hole, so a `}` left out of the inner string's hole ends the inner
// string at the quote meant for it, on a line that ends there; on a line
// with a later quote, the inner string runs to that one instead.
fn f(a: int) -> str = "{ "{a" }
fn g(a: int) -> str = "{ "{a" } tail"
